TVGlow change to zvbi v0.2.46 (34bb6f660c5c1bacd4a66cc7b22311e4ca3c1ab5),
used under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2 or later.

Purpose: build libzvbi from its LGPL files only, so that no GPL code reaches
libmpv-2.dll. zvbi's COPYING.md licenses src/packet-830.* and src/pdc.*
under GPL-2, and src/exp-vtx.c carries a GPL-2+ header. This patch stops
building them and removes every use of them:

- src/Makefile.am: the three files leave libzvbi_la_SOURCES, and pdc.h and
  packet-830.h leave the headers concatenated into libzvbi.h.
- src/packet.c: Teletext packet 8/30 format 1 (local time) and format 2
  (PDC) are ignored, and VPS program IDs are not decoded. Teletext pages
  and subtitles do not use them.
- src/vps.c, src/vps.h: the PDC encode and decode functions are removed.
- src/vbi.h, src/vbi.c, src/event.h: the program-ID members, their use and
  the pdc.h include are removed; event.h now includes network.h, which it
  used to get through pdc.h.
- src/libzvbi.h (checked in, normally generated): the same removals.

Lost: the VBI_EVENT_LOCAL_TIME and VBI_EVENT_PROG_ID events. FFmpeg's
teletext decoder registers neither.

